= December 2024 — One Left candidate or two?

Biejat can represent the governing Left while Zandberg runs for Razem, or the
party can reopen the nomination in search of one candidate. Either choice will
show whether the October split is an orderly separation or an unfinished
leadership fight.

- @biejat_confirm
- @biejat_primary
- @biejat_zandberg

@biejat_confirm
title: Confirm Biejat and let Razem run separately
on-arrival: pres_2025_left_candidate = "Magdalena Biejat"; pres_2025_candidate = "Magdalena Biejat"; pres_2025_razem_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg"; pres_2025_united_left = 0; pres_2025_campaign_strength += 1; progressives_dissent -= 2; razem_cooperation -= 3; news_headline = "Two Left candidacies prepare to measure government and opposition"
go-to: poland_event_queue

@biejat_primary
title: Reopen the decision through a Left-wide primary
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Outcome follows organisation, trust and a random electorate.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: There is no time or money for a credible primary.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 2;
Q.pres_2025_primary_roll =
    this.random.uint32() / 4294967296;
const zandbergScore =
    (Number(Q.razem_strength) || 0) +
    (Number(Q.labor_credibility) || 0) * 0.25 +
    (Number(Q.razem_cooperation) || 0) * 0.15 +
    Q.pres_2025_primary_roll * 15;
const biejatScore =
    (Number(Q.progressives_strength) || 0) +
    (Number(Q.spring_strength) || 0) * 0.45 +
    (Number(Q.progressive_credibility) || 0) * 0.20 +
    (1 - Q.pres_2025_primary_roll) * 15;
Q.pres_2025_left_candidate =
    zandbergScore > biejatScore ? "Adrian Zandberg" : "Magdalena Biejat";
Q.pres_2025_candidate = Q.pres_2025_left_candidate;
Q.pres_2025_razem_candidate = "None";
Q.pres_2025_united_left = 1;
Q.pres_2025_campaign_strength += 5;
Q.party_unity += 4;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.pres_2025_left_candidate + " wins an open Left primary";
!}
go-to: poland_event_queue

